description:
In blob.rs blob_download, the synthetic RFC 5322 message is returned with Content-Type: message/rfc822 but no Content-Length header. RFC 8620 §6.2 recommends that blob download responses include Content-Length. More concretely, the base64-encoded body may contain a 
 at the end of the format!() string, which results in a MIME entity that is not well-formed (the Content-Transfer-Encoding: base64 body should not have a trailing bare 
). The format string ends with {b64}
 which appends a CRLF after the base64 — base64 bodies should end at the last encoded character without trailing CRLF.
